# Bookshelf Data Structure Project\
\
A modern C++17 implementation of a type-safe bookshelf data structure that organizes values by C++ type. Each type gets its own "shelf" (a `TypedShelf`) which can operate in either sorted or unsorted modes.\
\
## Features\
\
- **Type-Safe Storage**: Store different types in the same data structure\
- **Dual-Mode Shelves**: Each type can have both sorted and unsorted shelves\
- **Binary Search**: Fast lookups in sorted shelves using binary search\
- **Range Queries**: Get all values within a range [lower, upper]\
- **Min/Max Operations**: O(1) min/max retrieval from sorted shelves\
- **Modern C++**: Leverages C++17 features like `constexpr if` and structured bindings\
\
## Project Structure\
\
```\
bookshelf-dsa-project/\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ CMakeLists.txt              # CMake configuration\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ README.md                   # This file\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ include/                    # Header files\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ Bookshelf.hpp           # Main bookshelf class\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ TypedShelf.hpp          # Template class for type-specific shelves\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ ShelfInfo.hpp           # Metadata about shelves\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ ShelfEntry.hpp          # Shelf entry structure\
âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ src/                        # Implementation files\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ main.cpp                # Demo application\
âƒ´‚   âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ Bookshelf.cpp           # Implementation of non-template methods\
âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ test/                       # Test files\
    âƒ´ƒ¼âƒ´€âƒ´€ test_typed_shelf.cpp    # Unit tests for TypedShelf\
    âƒ´ƒ´âƒ´€âƒ´€ test_bookshelf.cpp      # Unit tests for Bookshelf\
```\
\
## Building\
\
### Prerequisites\
- C++17 compatible compiler (GCC 7+, Clang 5+, MSVC 2017+)\
- CMake 3.10 or higher\
\
### Build Instructions\
\
```bash\
cd /path/to/bookshelf-dsa-project\
mkdir build\
cd build\
cmake ..\
make\
```\
\
### Run Application\
\
```bash\
./bin/bookshelf_app\
```\
\
### Run Tests\
\
```bash\
./bin/tests/test_typed_shelf\
./bin/tests/test_bookshelf\
```\
\
Or run all tests with:\
\
```bash\
make test\
```\
\
## Class Overview\
\
### TypedShelf<T, Sorted>\
\
A template class that stores values of a single type T.\
\
**Features:**\
- Sorted mode (Sorted=true): Maintains elements in sorted order\
- Unsorted mode (Sorted=false): Maintains insertion order\
- Requires `operator<` for comparisons in sorted mode\
\
**Key Methods:**\
- `void add(const T& value)` - Add a value\
- `bool remove(const T& value)` - Remove a value\
- `bool contains(const T& value)` - Check if value exists\
- `const T& min()` - Get minimum (O(1) for sorted)\
- `const T& max()` - Get maximum (O(1) for sorted)\
- `std::list<T> getRange(const T& lower, const T& upper)` - Range query\
\
### Bookshelf\
\
The main data structure that manages multiple TypedShelves.\
\
**Features:**\
- Type-safe storage of mixed types\
- Support for both sorted and unsorted shelves per type\
- Alphabetical ordering of shelves when printing\
- Metadata tracking (elementCount, isSorted flag)\
\
**Key Methods:**\
- `template<T> void add(const T& value)` - Add to sorted shelf\
- `template<T> void addUnsorted(const T& value)` - Add to unsorted shelf\
- `template<T> bool remove(const T& value)` - Remove from either shelf\
- `template<T> std::list<T> getAll()` - Get all values of type T\
- `template<T> bool contains(const T& value)` - Check if value exists\
- `template<T> const T& min()` - Get minimum\
- `template<T> const T& max()` - Get maximum\
- `void print(bool detail=false)` - Print all shelves\
\
## Usage Example\
\
```cpp\
#include "Bookshelf.hpp"\
#include <iostream>\
#include <string>\
\
int main() {}\
    Bookshelf bookshelf;\
\
    // Add different types\
    bookshelf.add(5);\
    bookshelf.add(2);\
    bookshelf.add(10);\
    \
    bookshelf.add(3.14);\
    bookshelf.add(2.71);\
    \
    bookshelf.add(std::string("hello"));\
    bookshelf.add(std::string("world"));\
\
    // Check if value exists\
    if (bookshelf.contains(5)) {}\
        std::cout << "Found 5!" << std::endl;\
    }\
\
    // Get min/max\
    std::cout << "Integer range: [" "]"\
              << bookshelf.min<int>() << ", " \
              << bookshelf.max<int>() << "]" << std::endl;\
\
    // Get range\
    auto range = bookshelf.getRange(2, 8);\
    \
    // Print all\
    bookshelf.print(true);  // true for detailed output\
\
    return 0;\
}\
```\
\
## Time Complexity\
\
| Operation | Sorted Shelf | Unsorted Shelf |\
|-----------|--------------|----------------|\
| Add       | O(n)         | O(1)           |\
| Remove    | O(n)         | O(n)           |\
| Contains  | O(n)*        | O(n)           |\
| Find      | O(n)*        | O(n)           |\
| Min/Max   | O(1)         | O(n)           |\
| Get Range | O(k)         | O(n)           |\
\
*Due to std::list's sequential access, binary search is O(n) rather than O(log n)\
\
## Design Decisions\
\
1. **Template-Based**: TypedShelf is fully templated for type safety and performance\
2. **std::list**: Chosen for insertion efficiency in sorted shelves\
3. **std::type_index**: Used for runtime type identification\
4. **Dual Shelves**: Support for both sorted and unsorted modes per type\
5. **Alphabetical Sorting**: Shelves are printed in alphabetical order by type name\
\
